==Icelandic==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈrɛːka/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|ɛːka|lang=is}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|vreka|lang=non}} (the ''v'' had disappeared already in later Old West Norse), from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{recons|wrekaną|lang=gem-pro}}.

====Verb====
{{is-verb-strong|rak|ráku|rekið}}

# to [[drive]] (forward or away)
# to [[run]] (a farm, business, etc.)
# [[coerce]], [[drive]] (someone to do something)
# to [[hammer]], [[hit]] (iron)
# {{context|impersonal|lang=is}} to cause to [[drift]]
#: ''[[bátur|Bátinn]] ([[accusative|acc.]]) '''rak''' út á [[haf#Icelandic|haf]].''
#: The boat '''drifted''' out to sea.

